# 1. Arrays of Objects

Instead of creating project cards manually in HTML, I stored all project information inside an array of JavaScript objects.

Example:

```javascript
const projects = [

    {
        title: "Portfolio Website",
        description: "Responsive portfolio website.",
        category: "HTML/CSS",
        technologies: "HTML, CSS, JavaScript",
        github: "https://github.com/..."
    }

];
```

## Why Arrays of Objects?

- Organizes related information.
- Makes adding projects easier.
- Reduces repetitive HTML.
- Makes websites easier to maintain.

