# 17. Debugging

Today's biggest lesson was debugging.

Common Problems Found

## Duplicate Variables

Wrong

```javascript
let preferences = {};

let preferences = {};
```

Correct

```javascript
let preferences = {

    theme:"light",

    sort:"default",

    filter:"All",

    search:""

};
```

---

## Missing Functions

Calling

```javascript
savePreferences();
```

before creating

```javascript
function savePreferences(){}
```

causes JavaScript to stop running.

---

## Missing HTML Elements

JavaScript

```javascript
document.getElementById("projects-container")
```

requires

```html
<div id="projects-container"></div>
```

Without it, JavaScript returns

```javascript
null
```

---

## Invalid HTML

Wrong

```html
<option>JavaScript</option>
```

Correct

```html
<select>

<option>JavaScript</option>

</select>
```

---

## Missing Closing Tags

Always close every opening tag.

Examples

```html
</section>

</div>

</main>

</body>

</html>
```

Missing closing tags can prevent sections from displaying.

